<article class="env-proposition" id="0A7K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A7K">Proposition <span data-tag="0A7K">47.15.11</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring which has a dualizing complex. Then any $A$-algebra essentially of finite type over $A$ has a dualizing complex. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from a combination of Lemmas <a href="/tag/0A7G" data-tag="0A7G">47.15.6</a>, <a href="/tag/0A7I" data-tag="0A7I">47.15.9</a>, and <a href="/tag/0A7J" data-tag="0A7J">47.15.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>